The full rules are in AGENTS.md ("Model rules", "Changelog rules"). In short:

Models
- Training without --run-name creates <train.run_name>-v<model_version>; never put a -vN suffix in run_name.
- A run with merged/config.json is final: only evaluation may write calibration.json, eval.json, model_info.json there.
- Unfinished version: tell the owner to run `make resume` or `make restart`; do not delete it.
- model_version is raised only by `scripts/07_models.py bump` after the version completed.
- Requests without `model` resolve to the newest completed versioned model; `sanity` never becomes latest over a versioned model.
- Accuracy numbers come from `make evaluate` or telemetry and name the split, label set (72 merged / 100 original) and top-1 vs top-3.
- Changing label groups, base model, max_len or loss makes new versions non-comparable: record it in CHANGELOG.md and MEMORY.md.

Changelog
- Every user-visible change goes under [Unreleased] in CHANGELOG.md and changelog.html, same entries and order.
- Group as Added / Changed / Fixed / Removed / Deprecated / Security; mark breaking changes "Breaking"; list exact dependency versions.
- Releases: rename [Unreleased] to [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD, bump the package version, add a new empty [Unreleased].
